# Docs, ADRs, and memory

## Layout

| Path | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `.claude/memory/MEMORY.md` | Durable facts about the product and this program |
| `.claude/memory/CONTEXT.md` | What already shipped vs gaps (as of 2026-09-17) |
| `.claude/adr/NNN-*.md` | Architecture Decision Records |
| `docs/superpowers/specs/` | Design specs |
| `docs/superpowers/plans/` | Bite-sized implementation plans |
| `apps/orchestrator/docs/` | Product docs already in the app (`FEATURES.md`, `OVERVIEW.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`) |

## ADR format

Each ADR has: Status (`accepted` / `proposed` / `superseded`), Context, Decision, Consequences.

Do not silently reverse an `accepted` ADR. Open a new ADR that supersedes it.

## When implementing a plan

1. Read the matching spec + ADR first.
2. Follow existing files listed in the plan; do not invent a parallel stack.
3. After a slice ships, update `CONTEXT.md` (done vs remaining) and `CHANGELOG.md`.
